sentences.l:
And Polydamas himself avoided the black death-fate
darting aslant, and received it did Antenor’s son,
Archelochus;

sentences.t:
φράζεο Πουλυδάμα καί μοι νημερτὲς ἐνίσπες
ἦ ῥ’ οὐχ οὗτος ἀνὴρ Προθοήνορος ἀντὶ πεφάσθαι
ἄξιος;

sentences.l:
Not indeed to me base does he seem, nor from base ones,
but a brother of Antenor, the horse-taming,
or a son;

Consider how for you Promachus, subdued, sleeps
by my spear, so that in no way the requital for a brother, at least,
long unpaid may be;

and he wounded Ilioneus,
son of Phorbas, rich in flocks, whom then most
Hermes of the Trojans loved, and gave him property;

and the spear through the eye, on through,
and through the nape went, and he sat down, his two hands spreading
both;

and Peneleos, drawing his sharp sword,
struck the neck in the middle, and he knocked off to the ground
the head together with the helmet;

for not even she, the wife of Promachus, Alegenor’s-son,
will be glad at her dear husband’s coming, whenever indeed
from Troy with our ships we return, the youths of the Achaeans.”

And Atreus’-son then Hyperenor, shepherd of the people,
wounded in the flank, and through, the bowels, the bronze drew out,
having cut him down;
